{
  "source": "video-audit/be-curious-rerolls-2026-11-04/audio-checks/existing-habits.wav",
  "duration": 48.2,
  "segments": [
    {
      "start": 0.0,
      "end": 6.28,
      "text": "The first habit is to use AI regularly, especially outside of your required schoolwork."
    },
    {
      "start": 6.86,
      "end": 12.28,
      "text": "This baseline familiarity makes it much easier to notice when an interface suddenly gains new abilities."
    },
    {
      "start": 13.1,
      "end": 18.44,
      "text": "Next, you should check what changed. Look out for update notices, new buttons, or model names."
    },
    {
      "start": 19.1,
      "end": 23.52,
      "text": "Constant monitoring isn't necessary. Checking occasionally gives you the information you need."
    },
    {
      "start": 24.12,
      "end": 27.58,
      "text": "To avoid feeling overwhelmed, follow one reliable source."
    },
    {
      "start": 27.58,
      "end": 32.26,
      "text": "Pick a single trustworthy newsletter, educator, or official product page."
    },
    {
      "start": 32.92,
      "end": 37.82,
      "text": "Calling your inputs down to one curated feed provides enough information to stay informed."
    },
    {
      "start": 38.64,
      "end": 44.06,
      "text": "Finally, compare with others. Ask your friends, teachers, or club members what they have tried recently."
    },
    {
      "start": 44.8,
      "end": 47.84,
      "text": "Different people naturally stumble upon different tools and features."
    }
  ],
